title: BYOTC - Trusted Security Process Injection Abusing Kernel Driver
id: 6d8e0f2a-4b6c-4d8e-a0f2-4b6c8d0e2f4a
status: experimental
description: Detects process injection into signed security applications to abuse kernel driver trust relationships (Bring Your Own Trusted Caller). Attackers inject code into legitimate security processes (e.g. Malwarebytes) that have trusted access to kernel drivers with sensitive capabilities like ZwTerminateProcess.
references:
  - https://cyberpress.org/windows-attack-hijacks-trusted-security-apps-to-abuse-powerful-kernel-drivers/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1055
  - attack.t1574
logsource:
  category: process_access
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_target:
    TargetImage|endswith: '\\mbamchameleon.sys'
    OR TargetImage|contains: 'mbamchameleon'
  selection_injection:
    GrantedAccess|contains:
      - '0x1410'
      - '0x1FFFFF'
      - '0x1F0FFF'
  selection_zwterminate:
    TargetImage|contains: 'Malwarebytes'
    CallTrace|contains: 'ZwTerminateProcess'
  condition: selection_target and selection_injection or selection_zwterminate
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate security software operations (Malwarebytes self-protection)
level: medium
